
========================================================================
A  THM-2053: a determinant certificate in chosen Euclidean coordinates
========================================================================
  n=13; det(c_1,c_2)=1, so the displayed basis is saturated; u+z has positive support.
  certificate: 91*max_i|a*z_i-b*u_i| <= a^2+b^2  ==>  M(a*u+b*z) >= 1/14
  a^2+b^2 is the chosen-coordinate Euclidean form [1,0,1], discriminant -4.
  It is not a plane-intrinsic form of discriminant -7 and changes under a GL(2,Z) basis change.
  d=(  30,   1): max|det|=  148; norm/91=      9.9; certified=False
  d=( 200,   3): max|det|=  994; norm/91=    439.7; certified=False
  d=( 700, 700): max|det|= 2100; norm/91=  10769.2; certified=True
  d=(2000,   1): max|det|= 9998; norm/91=  43956.1; certified=True

========================================================================
B  Exact failure carrier: a union of 26 open tangent disks
========================================================================
  columns=13 give 2n=26 disks; every disk has the origin on its boundary.
  exact round envelope: a^2+b^2 < 91^2*34 = 281554.
  checked all 537776 primitive nonzero lattice points in that envelope.
  uncertified points=348600, or 174300 directions modulo d~-d; disk/gate tests agree exactly.
  'Uncertified' is not 'unsafe': THM-2053 gives a sufficient certificate, not an equivalence.

========================================================================
C  Independent classical check: selected imaginary-quadratic class numbers
========================================================================
  discriminant   -3: class number 1
  discriminant   -4: class number 1
  discriminant   -7: class number 1
  discriminant   -8: class number 1
  discriminant  -11: class number 1
  discriminant  -15: class number 2
  discriminant  -19: class number 1
  discriminant  -20: class number 2
  discriminant  -23: class number 3
  discriminant  -43: class number 1
  discriminant  -67: class number 1
  discriminant -163: class number 1
  In particular h(-7)=1.  This classifies forms of discriminant -7 only.
  The THM-2053 coordinate norm above has discriminant -4, and its 26 translated disks are not
  ideal classes or equivalence classes of binary quadratic forms.  No atlas compression follows.

========================================================================
D  Legendre-symbol audit: (-p/p)=0, while (-1/p) is a different symbol
========================================================================
  p= 3: (-p/p)=+0; (-1/p)=-1
  p= 5: (-p/p)=+0; (-1/p)=+1
  p= 7: (-p/p)=+0; (-1/p)=-1
  p=11: (-p/p)=+0; (-1/p)=-1
  p=13: (-p/p)=+0; (-1/p)=+1
  Because p divides the discriminant -p, (disc/p)=0, not +/-1.
  The separate identity (-1/p)=(-1)^((p-1)/2) records p mod 4; it is not (disc/p).

========================================================================
E  Scope of the surviving observation
========================================================================
  SURVIVES: determinant identity; quadratic-vs-linear safe tail; exact 26-disk failure carrier;
            finite primitive residual for each chosen basis; classical class-number table.
  DOES NOT FOLLOW: an LRC14 discriminant -7; a Paley-to-plane identification; rank= isotropic;
                   Euler=anisotropic; anisotropic=>lonely; or class-number-one atlas compression.
  Remaining LRC14 work is still to construct/compress the actual plane atlas and discharge each
  plane's exact tangent-disk lattice points by a valid loneliness argument.
